  "body": "## What changed\n\nFive-axis generators set the first station's pose on the modal builder\nand then pushed the descend to first contact, so the rotary swing rode\nthe approach move: the machine turned the A/C head while the tool\ndescended, and the ball swept through unknown air and through the rim\nit approached.\n\nThe fix splits the approach. The pose is stated as its own zero-travel\nRapid (a standstill rotary index - the tip held on the hop plane, or at\nthe tip the machine already holds), and the Plunge/cut descends under\nthe pose already stated:\n\n- `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/curve.rs` (`contour_curve`): every\n  chain's approach swings first, then plunges.\n- `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/stamp.rs` (the stamp emit loop, all\n  posed kinds - parallel5d, flow5d, swarf5d, rough, contour5d): at\n  every rapid-to-cut re-entry where the pose changes, the swing is\n  emitted at a standstill before the cut. Intermediate cut moves keep\n  the modal tilt law unchanged.\n\nNo new `MoveKind`. The builder already keeps a zero-travel move whose\npose changed (it drops one only when the tip AND the pose both stand),\nand the post already solves a zero-travel segment as a pure rotary\nreorientation (`ds_tip == 0` in `crates/post/src/post/g93.rs`), so the\nswing always commands. That is the answer to the zero-travel question:\nthe swing is a zero-travel rapid, not a short travel move - a travel\nmove would drag the tip sideways while the head turns, and a dropped\nzero-travel move cannot occur, because a drop needs the pose to match\nthe held one, in which case no rotation is due.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 28 steps, 0 failed\n  (motion lib 536 passed, multiaxis, multiaxis_avoid, multiaxis_rough,\n  pivot5d, swarf_pose_continuity, app operations, posed_contact and the\n  rest all green).\n- The existing laws were amended where the swing touches them, each in\n  its own terms: a TRAVEL rapid still inherits its pose\n  (`rapids_hold_the_pose_they_inherit`, `rapid_pose_contract` - the\n  zero-travel index is the second legal way a rapid states a pose,\n  beside the swarf link's ball-centred swing); the air-link ratchet\n  counts travel links only; the pivot-law ball readers skip the\n  swing (it cuts nothing) through `no_swings`/`sans_swings` helpers.\n- A decision record sits in `docs/decisions/3414-approach-rotary-order.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `the_approach_rotates_before_it_descends` (crates/motion/tests/pivot5d.rs):\n  a zero-travel rotary swing precedes the first descend; the plunge\n  holds the pose the swing stated; no pose change rides any move that\n  crosses from air to material, over contour_curve, parallel5d, flow5d\n  and swarf5d.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- No posted G-code golden was regenerated (the post's pure-rotary path\n  is covered by its own suite; the swing was not posted end to end on\n  a real machine file).\n- The heavy lanes were not run; the diff touches `camcraft-motion`, so\n  the release-tier lane check stays with the review/cut.\n\n## Changelog\n\nFive-axis approach moves rotate the machine to the first pose before\nthe tool descends to the part, no longer while it descends.\n\nFork synced at v0.25.0.\n\nFixes #3414\n",
